{"name":"Hunt Club","hex":"#2a4f43","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hunt","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To find or search for an animal in the wild with the intention of killing the animal for its meat or for sport.","To try to find something; search (for)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of hunting.","A hunting expedition."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunt"},{"term":"club","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A heavy object, often a kind of stick, intended for use as a bludgeoning weapon or a plaything.\n\n An implement to hit the ball in certain ball games, such as golf.\n An item used during routines, the apparatus consisting of a set of two clubs.","An implement to hit the ball in certain ball games, such as golf."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit with a club.","To score a victory over by a large margin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/club"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hunt Club","blocks":[{"text":"Hunt Club is a community in River Ward, in the south end of Ottawa, Ontario, Canada. The area is named after the Ottawa Hunt and Golf Club, which was first developed in 1876. Hunt Club Road and many local businesses were also named after the golf course."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Hunt_Club-Riverside_Park_Community_Centre%2C_Ottawa.jpg/330px-Hunt_Club-Riverside_Park_Community_Centre%2C_Ottawa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunt_Club","wikidata":"Q5943920"},{"title":"Hunt Club Road","blocks":[{"text":"Hunt Club Road, also known as Ottawa Road 32, is a major east–west route in Ottawa, Ontario, Canada. It originally ran from a dead end east of Bank Street to the Ottawa Hunt and Golf Club; later, there were many extensions due to the 1970s housing boom, first westward to Riverside Drive, then eastward to Hawthorne Road in the late 1980s. The section between Bank Street and Riverside Drive, originally only one lane in each direction, was expanded to two lanes in each direction in 1993–1994. It was further extended across the Rideau River and the southern edge of the suburbs to Old Richmond Road by the late 1990s; this extension is signed as West Hunt Club Road by the City of Ottawa. Construction to extend Hunt Club eastward to Highway 417 near Ramsayville was completed on 21 August 2014."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Hunt_Club.jpg/330px-Hunt_Club.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunt_Club_Road","wikidata":"Q5943925"},{"title":"Hunt Club (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Hunt Club is a 2023 American action thriller film written by David Lipper and John F. Saunders, directed by Elizabeth Blake-Thomas and starring Mena Suvari, Mickey Rourke and Casper Van Dien."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ac/Hunt_Club_pic.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunt_Club_(film)","wikidata":"Q117842613"},{"title":"Hunting","blocks":[{"text":"Hunting is the human practice of seeking, pursuing, capturing, and/or killing wildlife or feral animals. The most common reasons for humans to hunt are to obtain the animal's body to consume their meat and useful animal products, for recreation/taxidermy, although it may also be done for other purposes such as removing predators dangerous to humans or domestic animals, to eliminate pests and nuisance animals that damage crops/livestock/poultry or spread diseases, for trade/tourism, or for ecological conservation against overpopulation and invasive species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Paul_Childerley_driven_hunt_Finland_04.png/330px-Paul_Childerley_driven_hunt_Finland_04.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunting","wikidata":"Q36963"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg/500px-Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg/1280px-Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg/500px-Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bowhunter with a compound bow using a call","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Professional_stalker_standing_next_to_red_deer_stag_Ardnamurchan_Estate_Scotland_darker_01.png/500px-Professional_stalker_standing_next_to_red_deer_stag_Ardnamurchan_Estate_Scotland_darker_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Professional_stalker_standing_next_to_red_deer_stag_Ardnamurchan_Estate_Scotland_darker_01.png/1280px-Professional_stalker_standing_next_to_red_deer_stag_Ardnamurchan_Estate_Scotland_darker_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Professional_stalker_standing_next_to_red_deer_stag_Ardnamurchan_Estate_Scotland_darker_01.png/500px-Professional_stalker_standing_next_to_red_deer_stag_Ardnamurchan_Estate_Scotland_darker_01.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Professional deerstalker standing over a downed red stag in Scotland","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AProfessional_stalker_